    "body": "Thank you all for attending this meeting and especially to Chris Wilson for running it in my absence! Here are the belated notes from this meeting (the next one is at https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9591):\r\n\r\n### Agenda  \r\nAttendees: Joey Arhar, Ryosuke Niwa, Kagami Rosylight, Keith Cirkel, L David Baron, Peter Van der Beken, Chris Wilson, Emilio Cobos Álvarez\r\n\r\n1. Review past action items\r\n    1. Brian will address review feedback on [Update the :dir / directionality to include shadow dom](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9166). \r\n        1. [not present]\r\n    1. Yi will review [Reference even more baseline concepts in CSS Inline Layout](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5826).\r\n        1. [not present]\r\n    1. Mason will add the \"addition/proposal\" label to the non-blocking [issues for Popover](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22topic%3A+popover%22).\r\n        1. [Done](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9474#issuecomment-1634804056).\r\n1. Carryovers from last time\r\n    1. None.\r\n1. New topics\r\n    1. [Anne] [Add custom state pseudo class](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8467)\r\n        1. CSS WG had some meetings to talk about : state vs : dash; seems like they prefer state; Ryosuke suggests bringing up in the CSSWG.  Joey points to [https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/4805](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/4805) for agenda+ing, Emilio agenda+ed.\r\n\r\n### Action Items\r\n\r\n1. None",
